      <activity id="3fd96576-acc3-5f0c-8cb8-2b2403a21f34" activityNameId="ee52b66e-b582-5678-b014-3519ade75d36" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, high voltage, operation storage pumps, ENTSO, 2020, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, high voltage, operation storage pumps, ENTSO, 2020, at grid
Transmission losses are taken from Itten, Frischknecht and Stucki (2014): LCI of Electricity Mixes and Grid.; UUID:9d2751da-9114-3e85-9726-3f21810c1d21
This dataset describes the transmission of the electricity mix used for the operation of storage pumps in Germany in 2018 and includes the high voltage network infrastructure (including long-distance transport), transmission losses and air pollutant emissions. Not included are electricity losses due to long-distance transport since they are assumed to be contained in the total electricity losses of the country network.
Location: Germany
Technology: Average technology
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: 
Sampling: Statistics
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9d2751da-9114-3e85-9726-3f21810c1d21.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
